-- title:
--   Newform K(q)-invariants embed into the dual Tate module
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'\ge 1$ a natural number not divisible by $q$, and $\lambda$ a prime, with $\mathbb{C}$ equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra structure. Assume: `LevelAutInputs q M'`, i.e. for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ an automorphism of the field `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ exists satisfying the $q$-expansion identity `IsLevelAutBar` for slashing by `conjElem q γ`; `HeckeGenCommute q M'`, i.e. the endomorphisms `heckeGenJac q M' ℓ` of `Jac q M'` commute pairwise; `GL2Laws q M'`, i.e. a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ to $\mathrm{End}(\mathrm{Jac}\,q\,M')$ exists carrying reductions of $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ to `slJac q M' γ` and `diagOneElem q d` to `diagJac q M' d`; and `HeckeDiamondInputsHAll` for level $q^2M'$ with $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction of unit groups, i.e. the Hecke inputs along every prime together with diamond automorphisms for every $d$. Let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$ which is a newform (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem agrees with none occurring at a proper divisor of the level), and let $\Phi$ be an adelic lift of $g$ in the sense of `IsAdelicLiftOf`. Let $V$ be a complex vector space with a distributive action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ commuting with the scalars, and $f\colon V\to$ [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan Φ`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) an injective $\mathbb{C}$-linear $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-equivariant map whose range is the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-orbit of `AdelicSpan.self Φ`. Then there is an injective $\mathbb{C}$-linear map $\psi$ from the submodule of vectors of $V$ fixed by [`FLT.SmoothVectors.gl2CongruenceSubgroup q 1`](def/RepTheory_GL2CongruenceSubgroup.html#L181) to the $\mathbb{C}$-dual of $\mathbb{C}\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T_\lambda(\mathrm{Jac}\,q\,M')$ such that, first, for every $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and every fixed vector $v$, $\psi$ of `gl2ReductionRep q V x v` equals the dual map of the base change to $\mathbb{C}$ of `tateGL2 q M' lam x⁻¹` applied to $\psi v$, and second, for every prime $\ell$ the dual map of the base change of `tateHecke q M' lam (heckeGen ℓ)` sends $\psi v$ to $c_\ell\,\psi v$, where $c_\ell=0$ if $\ell\mid qM'$ and $c_\ell$ is the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the cohomological form of the Eichler–Shimura comparison at full level $q$: the $K(q)$-invariant vectors of the local representation generated by the adelic lift of the newform $g$ are realised, contragrediently for the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$-action and with transposed Hecke operators acting by the coefficients $a_\ell(g)$, inside the dual of the complexified $\lambda$-adic Tate module of the full-level Jacobian. It feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ringHom_heckeGen_eq_and_exists_ne_zero_comm_baseChange_tateModule_jac`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ringHom_heckeGen_eq_and_exists_ne_zero_comm_baseChange_tateModule_jac), which extracts from it the Hecke ring homomorphism and a nonzero vector in the Tate module used later in the construction of the Galois representation attached to $g$.
